zoe: heads-up: new edge starter sample fails type inference after the bundle step. generic on our sdk helper becomes `any` for consumer code. only when built for edge.
mike: link to minimal repro? curious if it's our d.ts or esbuild/swc behavior.
zoe: tiny repro below — works in node but after edge bundling the consumer sees `any`:
```ts
// lib/client.ts
export type Policy<T = unknown> = { delay?: number; meta?: T }
export function secure<T>(opts: Policy<T>): { run: () => T }
export function secure(opts: Policy<any>) { return { run: () => (opts.meta as any) } }

// app/index.ts
const s = secure({ meta: { id: 42 } })
// expect s.run() => { id: number } but TS shows any when built for edge
```
lee: sounds like implementation signature leaked into published .d.ts. we ship dual outputs and an exports map; bundler + moduleResolution:bundler can cause TS to pick the wrong declaration surface.
doc-bot: created DX-4601: "edge bundle -> generic overload widens to any in examples" (assign: @mike).
mike: quick mitigation: update example tsconfig to `moduleResolution: node16` and add note in README. stable fix: ensure published declarations expose only `declare` overloads and hide impl via `/** @internal */` + `stripInternal: true`. also explicitly set `types` paths in exports map to reduce resolver ambiguity.
harper: another defensive option: change public defaults to `unknown` and provide a narrowing helper `narrowPolicy<T>(p: Policy<T>): Policy<T>` so consumers opt-in. less ideal but non-breaking.
lee: agreed on `declare` overloads + strip internal; also add a CI step that runs `tsc --noEmit` for examples under both `bundler` and `node16`. catch it early.
zoe: i'll hold the sample PR until typings PR lands. i'll attach esbuild and vercel edge logs to DX-4601.
mike: ETA: will open PR with d.ts change + typing test tomorrow. will ping this thread when ready.
zoe: thanks all. added onboarding checklist item "edge typings smoke test" to devx docs.
